From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 15:32:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] windowscodecs: Interpolate in the bitmap scaler's linear,
 cubic, Fant and high quality cubic modes.

Every mode but nearest neighbour was drawn as nearest neighbour, and
PowerPoint scales pictures with Fant.  For formats with 8-bit, 16-bit or
float channels the scaler now resamples separably at each destination
pixel's centre: linear and cubic (Keys, a = -1/2) weigh the 2 and 4
nearest source pixels, high quality cubic widens the cubic kernel by the
reduction, and Fant averages the source pixels a reduced pixel covers
and enlarges linearly; edge pixels repeat.  Indexed and packed formats
stay nearest neighbour.  The kernels' exact details are not measured on
Windows yet; the tests only check what any interpolation gives.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

